# Copy to .env.local and fill in from Supabase → Project Settings → API keys.
#
# These two are PUBLIC by design. The publishable key ships to every visitor's browser
# and identifies the project; it grants nothing on its own. Row Level Security is what
# protects the data, which is why every table has policies rather than relying on key
# secrecy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# --- Server-side only. NEVER commit these, and never prefix them with VITE_ ---
# Set in Netlify → Site settings → Environment variables. A VITE_ prefix would bake the
# value into a browser bundle, which is exactly what must not happen to the last two.
#
#   SUPABASE_URL                same project URL, read by netlify/functions/login-mobile.js
#   SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY    same public key; login-mobile.js signs the user in with it
#                               so the session is an ordinary RLS-bound one
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY         bypasses RLS entirely — full read/write on every yuvak's
#                               data. Two functions use it, both narrowly:
#                               login-mobile.js to resolve a mobile number to an email,
#                               and publish-drive-image-background.js to write the encoded
#                               image into Storage and update the scene. That second one
#                               checks the caller holds `darshan.publish` — using the
#                               caller's own token, never this key — before it does
#                               anything, because a background function is a public
#                               endpoint that answers 202 to everyone.
#   SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD        the Postgres password, used by scripts/db.mjs to apply
#                               migrations. Full database access; pass it from the
#                               environment for a single command, never write it to a file.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
